CL
;15                       Jimmy X
8  Instructions
;3        Welcome to
;4  Jimmy X,
3  the next generation in the Jimmy line of games.
  First you will need to run the setup program. to do this, go into your
  Jimmy directory and type
CR
  jsetup
CR
  at the Dos prompt.
  Press a key for more instructions

WT
CL
8      Now, a breif overview of this game.  The object is to destroy Bob, the
;8 universal badguy for Jimmy games.  If you played
;15  Jimmy 2,
8  (which you probably
  haven't), you know that Jimmy kills Bob, OR SO HE THOUGHT. Jimmy starts out
  in the feilds, with no money and no hope.  But, with your help, maybe Jimmy
  can become a hero once again. Maybe......
WT
CL
15   During Battle:
CR
7        The game is pretty simple.  Jimmy moves in between different areas,
  and makes a choice from a menu in each area.  From time to time, Jimmy will
  run into an Enemy.  Enemies are bad.  Enemies KILL Jimmy. Jimmy must kill
  enemies.
         Whenever you run into an enemy, you see a new menu.  In the very top
  center of the screen you will see a number start from 10 and count down.
  This is how much time you have remaining to make a choice.  If you don't
  make a choice and the counter runs down to ZERO, your enemy will attack, not
  letting you attack them at all(how rude).
CR
         In the top left is Jimmy's Hit points and Magic points.  Jimmy has a
  certain amount of Hitpoints, that increases whenever he goes up a level(see
  the section on going up levels). Whenever he is hit by an enemy, Jimmy loses
  a few hit points, until his hitpoints reach 0 - then he is dead.  Hitpoints
  also known as Hp, can be restored several different ways.  Mp(Magic points)
  go down every time jimmy casts a magic spell. If he doesn't have enough Mp
  for a spell, he can't use that spell.
WT
CL       In the top right is your enemy's Hp.  Every time you attack them,
  this will go down untill they are dead at ZERO.
         When you kill an enemy, you will get a certian amount of money and
  experience points.
CRNOTE: if you are having problems with the menu during battle, make sure that
        NumLock is OFF and you are using the # keys on top of the Keyboard,
  NOT the ones in the keypad.
WT
CL
15  Moving around:
CR
7 Different areas have different Menus.  All you do is pick a number from the
;7 menu and VOIALA!!
8 no other explanation is necesary.
WT
15
CL  Managing Yourself:
CR
7 You can se all of your vital statistics at anytime by simply typing in
;15 info
7  at one of the menus. Now let's talk about what all that stuff
  really means
CR
;3 Weapon:
7  The current weapon you have (strength determines how
  much damage it will do to an enemy)
CR
;3 Armor:
7  Your current armor
CR
;3 Sheild:
7  What type of sheild you are carrying
CR
WT

